-In summary, the Procedure must take the form of a continuously numbered set of steps (i.e. use 1, 2, 3, 4 and so on, not 1.1, 1.2 etc.), with numbering continuing from subsection to subsection. There can only be one level of Subheading within the Procedure section, so please amend headings as necessary. If there are options of how to proceed at a particular numbered step, options A, B, C etc., can be used within that step, and within the options, different steps should be numbered using roman numerals. If there are any optional/additional procedures that do not necessarily fit into the continuous flow of numbered steps which should be completed in order, these can be put into boxes as optional procedures and referred to from the Procedure as appropriate. Notice that the text in the Procedure of the example protocol (https://rdcu.be/eumxY) is either part of a numbered step OR part of a callout (CAUTION, CRITICAL STEP etc). While it is possible to include some explanatory text immediately under subheadings, please consider whether it would be better for the user to have this information before they start the Procedure i.e. to move some of the text to an appropriate section of the Introduction e.g. Experimental Design.\
